    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for a high-ceiling Saturday, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Andy Pages** (69.97). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter with Chandler, boasting a 4.92 xERA that drives a 19% boost to his base projection, while his spot in the two-hole amplifies his overall efficiency. Similarly, **Andy Pages** draws a soft matchup against the left-handed Sears (5.11 xERA); despite facing a southpaw, his elite power profile and high-leverage lineup position make him a primary engine for our offensive output today. **Gunnar Henderson** (69.41) and **Coby Mayo** (65.56) round out our top-tier tier, utilizing the weak pitching of Lodolo to overcome standard platoon hurdles.\n\nWhile our starters are well-positioned, **Heliot Ramos** (58.19) remains a high-interest play; he is currently benefiting from a massive 14% park factor boost, helping to mitigate a slightly tougher matchup against Gordon. The most difficult personnel decision today involved **Denzer Guzman** (44.48) on the bench. He hovered just outside our starting five, but his proximity to the 40.0 efficiency floor made him the odd man out in favor of the higher-projected **Sam Antonacci** (62.96), whose prime spot at the top of the lineup against Bibee provides better cumulative category potential. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Drake Baldwin** (51.03), who faces a tough test in McLean; his score is currently dampened by the opposing pitcher's 3.47 xERA and a heavy penalty for the SP skill match-up. Additionally, with **Jordan Westburg** currently sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested. Owners should keep a close eye on any late weather reports, though currently, the lineup logic remains stable. We are prioritizing speed and high-OBP roles today to keep the pressure on our opponents in the Stolen Base and Runs categories.",
